    "body": "Having just the focused buffer and a preview is my ideal setup but some file names tend to be long and can't be seen with fixed width limitation that currently exists.\r\n\r\nThis change introduces the ability to have dynamic buffer width which will be determined based on the longest line of that buffer.\r\n\r\nWith this feature added, my windows config is:\r\n```lua\r\n    windows = {\r\n      -- Maximum number of windows to show side by side\r\n      max_number = 2,\r\n      -- Whether to show preview of file/directory under cursor\r\n      preview = true,\r\n      -- Width of focused window\r\n      width_focus = 0,\r\n      -- Width of non-focused window\r\n      width_nofocus = 0,\r\n      -- Width of preview window\r\n      width_preview = 0,\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1728\" alt=\"Screenshot 2024-04-04 at 00 14 56\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/1770709/c887d1b7-b373-49b9-8764-5d1a64828125\">\r\n\r\nAs I'm using Mac, I couldn't add necessary tests\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-04-08T16:45:03Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI generally tried to avoid this type of dynamic window width based on the file content. For at least the following reasons:\r\n- Having as small width values as is reasonably possible is definitely the goal here, as it mean more windows can fit side-by-side on the screen.\r\n- Even single wide file name in the current buffer results into a wide window. Although that file might be invisible in the current window view.\r\n- Users can scroll horizontally with `zL` and `zH`, with special care put to ensure that this scrolled view is preserved during vertical scroll.\r\n\r\nI'll take time to think about this, but at the moment I have doubts this will be included.",
