        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Backwards compatibility is there, whoever wants to have fixed small width value can do so.\r\n> There aren't many people who are aware of zL and zH.\r\n> Maybe we can get to a compromise regarding the way this feature is enabled?\r\n> Instead of setting individual width props to 0 we can have a separate option like `dynamic_width: boolean` which will be applied to all three window types (nofocus, focus and preview)?\r\n\r\nBackwards compatibility is always a concern and it is indeed present here.\r\n\r\nWhat also is a primary concern is a \"functionality - maintainability\" balance. The 'mini.files' module is already quite big, both in terms of its functionality and lines of code. Adding more will mean more long-term maintenance, which also includes documentation and tests (which are needed plenty as there are quite a few edge cases to test).\r\n\r\nTogether with some usability concerns I expressed earlier, this currently makes me hesitant to add this.\r\n\r\n> One more question. Are contributions to this repo automatically applied to module specific repos as well? https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.files in this case\r\n\r\nIf merged, it will be applied later during (manual) synchronization.",
